{"id":10070,"name":"sharpedo-mega","speciesId":319,"dex":319,"form":"mega","generation":3,"types":["water","dark"],"stats":{"hp":70,"attack":140,"defense":70,"special-attack":110,"special-defense":65,"speed":105},"abilities":[{"name":"strong-jaw","hidden":false}],"height":25,"weight":1303,"baseExp":196,"sprites":{"normal":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/other/official-artwork/10070.png","shiny":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/other/official-artwork/shiny/10070.png","icon":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/10070.png"},"cry":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/cries/main/cries/pokemon/latest/10070.ogg","genus":"Brutal Pokémon","flavor":[{"version":"ruby","text":"Nicknamed “the bully of the sea,” SHARPEDO is widely feared. Its cruel fangs grow back immediately if they snap off. Just one of these POKéMON can thoroughly tear apart a supertanker."},{"version":"sapphire","text":"SHARPEDO can swim at speeds of up to 75 mph by jetting seawater out of its backside. This POKéMON’s drawback is its inability to swim long distances."},{"version":"emerald","text":"The vicious and sly gangster of the sea. Its skin is specially textured to minimize drag in water. Its speed tops out at over 75 miles per hour."},{"version":"firered","text":"The ruffian of the seas, it has fangs that crunch through iron. It swims by jetting water from its rear."},{"version":"diamond","text":"Its fangs rip through sheet iron. It swims at 75 mph and is known as “The Bully of the Sea.”"},{"version":"heartgold","text":"It can swim at speeds of 75 mph by jetting seawater through its body. It is the bandit of the sea."},{"version":"omega-ruby","text":"Nicknamed “the bully of the sea,” Sharpedo is widely feared. Its cruel fangs grow back immediately if they snap off. Just one of these Pokémon can thoroughly tear apart a supertanker."},{"version":"alpha-sapphire","text":"Sharpedo can swim at speeds of up to 75 mph by jetting seawater out of its backside. This Pokémon’s drawback is its inability to swim long distances."},{"version":"sun","text":"It pursues its prey at speeds of 75 mph and finishes them off with fangs that can crush iron. It is known as the bully of the sea."},{"version":"moon","text":"It has a sad history. In the past, its dorsal fin was a treasured foodstuff, so this Pokémon became a victim of overfishing."},{"version":"ultra-sun","text":"People believe that carrying one of its discarded fangs will prevent mishaps at sea, so the fangs are made into accessories."},{"version":"ultra-moon","text":"It drinks in seawater and jets it from its rear to propel itself. It’s very sensitive to the scent of blood."},{"version":"sword","text":"As soon as it catches the scent of prey, Sharpedo will jet seawater from its backside, hurtling toward the target to attack at 75 mph."},{"version":"shield","text":"This Pokémon is known as the Bully of the Sea. Any ship entering the waters Sharpedo calls home will be attacked—no exceptions."}],"genderRate":4,"captureRate":60,"eggGroups":["water2"],"isLegendary":false,"isMythical":false,"evolution":{"species":"carvanha","speciesId":318,"evolvesTo":[{"conditions":["Nível 30"],"species":"sharpedo","speciesId":319,"evolvesTo":[]}]},"varieties":[{"id":319,"name":"sharpedo","form":"normal","sprite":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/other/official-artwork/319.png"},{"id":10070,"name":"sharpedo-mega","form":"mega","sprite":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/other/official-artwork/10070.png"}],"games":[16,17,18],"moves":[{"id":43,"learn":[[16,"lv",1],[17,"lv",1],[18,"lv",1]]},{"id":44,"learn":[[16,"lv",1],[17,"lv",1],[18,"lv",1]]},{"id":46,"learn":[[16,"tm",0],[17,"tm",0],[18,"tm",0]]},{"id":57,"learn":[[16,"tm",0],[17,"tm",0],[18,"tm",0]]},{"id":58,"learn":[[16,"tm",0],[17,"tm",0],[18,"tm",0]]},{"id":59,"learn":[[16,"tm",0],[17,"